{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/799942-scenario-total-weaver-stasis-urbanisation-victory","id":799942,"title":"Scenario: Total Weaver/stasis/urbanisation victory.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-03T17:41:27-08:00","id":799942,"title":"Scenario: Total Weaver/stasis/urbanisation victory.","content":"(In case anyone who's playing my game is on here, you've got twenty years, and you shouldn't read any further)<br /> Scattering of thoughts<br /> <br /> A large portion of the Glass walkers become to the weaver what Black spirals are to the wyrm. I'll call em weaver walkers for now.<br /> This new faction offer information to the technocracy. Pentex and all of it's assets are seized.many of it's scientific advances added to the technocracy's already formidable understanding.<br /> Combined with this information and that fed by weaver walkers, The technocracy has enough scientific theory on garou to officially accept Weaver walkers into their ranks as non-reality deviants. (Unofficially, no. a large portion of the technocracy is unhappy with this, but given the cyborgs and genetic modifications going on, eventual acceptance is just as possible as betrayal)<br /> Using garou gifts such as sense wyrm, the weaver walkers eliminate nephandi influences in the technocracy.<br /> Weaver walkers lead hit teams on Caerns and hives alike. Pentex first teams were bad? Here we've got hit-marks,other robots,power armour, Mages,Traitorous Garou, Drones (The weaver equivalent of formori) Cyborgs and other enhanced humans, possibly including other man-made changing breeds. Neither stands a chance.Both should be wiped out within ten years. The Ratkin being a suicidal campaign that ultimately proves more suicide than campaign.<br /> With that out of the way. The traditions and the Vampires. The Sabbat, being a more obvious target, will be hunted down swiftly, but as in the inquisition; in all sects and clans the elders will last far longer than the neonates. Melding with the earth and escaping into torpor is an option, but with advancing technology, no vampire can hide.<br /> As with the traditions? The crafts? Weak. Just hunt them down.<br /> The fae? They'll die off without assistance.<br /> <br /> What's left?<br /> <br /> Garou: The bone gnawers (Best tribe). The shadowlords (and hakken) . Uktena.,that african hunting dog tribe, Siberkah And a few glass walkers came out best. a very small minority of the other tribes exist, but they're mostly in harano. Not sure if the Get would have survived or fought the hardest and died miserably. In this era, the Ragabash is king.<br /> No changing breed got wiped out, maybe some bastet were decimated, but most of them weren't visible enough to demand focused effort. On the plus side for garou, as tribes are decimated, their totems shift allegiances, each surviving tribe gets more favoured gifts.<br /> <br /> Mages; Orphans. Lots and lots of orphans. Technomancy becomes more and more common as old arts are seldom adapted. The technocracy snowballs in it's acquisition of new enlightened personnel. The traditions and the disparates might still exist, but they have no order, and<br /> <br /> Vampires<br /> Many are in torpor, waiting for the storm to go away. The masquerade is less that vampires exist, and more that vampires survived. Each clan is as common as the bloodlines, though Brujah,Tremere, setites and balli proved to be easier than others to hunt down. There is little interaction between neonate and elder. The elders sit in their towers, surrounded by guards, more paranoid than ever. The rest are actively hunted, like everything else.<br /> <br /> Faeries- Welcome to winter.<br /> <br /> Wraiths- I don't know squat about wraiths. Let's say the gauntlet is incredibly thick.<br /> <br /> These survivors have to work together or go it alone. 